title: Jazz in Six
key: Em
tempo: 88
meter: 6/8
style: jazz

// Jazz's six-eight: two pulses to the bar, three eighths in each, the ride on
// each pulse and the eighth before the next. Thirty-two bars, AABA, most
// chords two bars long. The A sits on the minor one and its four, and turns
// round by the minor two-five; the second and last A come home through the
// flat six. The bridge is the relative major's two-five-one and its four,
// and the minor two-five back, ending on the five with a sharp nine.
[A]
| Em9 | % | Am9 | % | Em9 | % | F#m7b5 | B7b9 |

[A2]
| Em9 | % | Am9 | % | Cmaj7 | F#m7b5 B7b9 | Em9 | % |

[Bridge]
| Am9 | D13 | Gmaj7 | Cmaj7 | F#m7b5 | B7b9 | Em9 | B7#9 |

[A3]
| Em9 | % | Am9 | % | Cmaj7 | F#m7b5 B7b9 | Em9 | % |
